<title>GERMANY: Russia paid $50 mln instalment under debt deal.</title>
<headline>Russia paid $50 mln instalment under debt deal.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Deutsche Bank AG said on Thursday Russia's Vnesheconombank last Monday transferred $50 million to a trust account held with the Bank of England, the final instalment of a cash downpayment made in accordance with a debt rescheduling pact agreed in principle in November 1995.</p>
<p>The payments made by Vnesheconombank since February 1995 now amount to two billion dollars, Deutsche Bank, which chairs the advisory committee of the London Club bank creditors for Russia, said in a statement.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
